    #      line names the superseded directory as
    #      <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p3-p1/superseded. Every rm -rf is on a
    #      directory this run made, written with ${var:?} (specs/0024,
    #      "Planning rulings during P2", ruling 1): the trap's mktemp directory,
    #      which holds the keep directory of change RD, and the shape fixture's.
    #  SB. The spec is specs/0025, pinned by its COMMITTED blob (c15d68d2...,
    #      the hash planning's message gave for the doc commit), at the phase
    #      commit. The working tree's copy holds planning's uncommitted rulings
    #      during P1 and is printed, not pinned; the entry guard and the status
    #      block allow that one line beside this phase's log directory and its
    #      record stems (records/m3p3-p1- and records/m3p3-open-).
    #  SC. As PC: the workspace run holds the sheetprops module's tests, so the
    #      feature sheetprops was on, beside the richtext, images, comments,
    #      tables, rules and metadata modules.
    #  SD. The crate's own tests with the feature sheetprops off and on, on both
    #      targets (in place of P3's four sets of richtext and comments): the on
    #      run's names are the off run's plus exactly the sheetprops module's,
    #      and the off run holds none of them.
    #  SE. The tests the source adds are derived from the diff, not typed (QE's
    #      form in place of RE): one new test file, package/tests/sheetprops.rs,
    #      every #[test] of which is new; one test added to
    #      package/tests/richtext.rs and one to package/tests/comments/rich.rs
    #      (the carry, specs/0024 close-out ruling 3), each named for the
    #      unbound prefix; and the tool's tests added to null_rewrite.rs, each
    #      named for the sheetview sample. No test file outside those four gains
